1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,360
Okay, here's what you need to know about Justin Pearson's path to reinstatement.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:07,040
Shelby County Commission will meet to decide whether or not to reappoint him

3
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,200
to represent his district here in Tennessee.

4
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:11,920
Nine of the 13 county commissioners are Democrats.

5
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,400
They hold a super majority on the county commission,

6
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:18,340
which means that things should go smoothly for him, but there are a few snags.

7
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,040
For starters, I spoke to Commissioner Sugarman today,

8
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:24,880
and she told me that two of the Democratic commissioners are out of town and won't be voting.

9
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:29,980
She also shared that she and other commissioners are worried about Tennessee Republicans retaliating.

10
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:33,520
That if the commission sends Justin Pearson back to the state's Capitol,

11
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:36,240
that Republicans may make them pay. Literally.

12
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:41,940
She's concerned that the Tennessee GOP will revoke funding for infrastructure and medical facilities.

13
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:45,000
It's unclear whether or not those concerns will materialize.

14
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:48,040
The Republican Speaker of the House has explicitly denied them,

15
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:51,420
but one thing is for sure, the nation will be watching how this vote plays out.

